message: "If you use AZM-QOS in academic work, please cite the associated software release and related manuscript when available."
title: "AZM-QOS: A Quantum Observable Simulation and QEC-Aware Research Workflow Platform"
version: "5.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20572833"
orcid id: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6957-7874
date-released: "06/06/2026"
authors:
  - family-names: "Momin"
    given-names: "Abdul Aziz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AzizMaz7/azm-qos"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - variational quantum simulation
  - quantum error correction
  - END/VQS
  - research software
abstract: >
  AZM-QOS is a Python-based research software platform for generalized quantum
  observable simulation workflows, QEC-aware logical estimators, hardware-result
  synchronization, reproducibility exports, and manuscript/thesis scaffolding.
